### Page 6 of 162

```text
JR?AL
good4u \
January 27, 2022
VIA UPS NEXT DAY
Cheyenne City Council
2101 O’Neil Avenue
Cheyenne, WY 82001
Re:
Retail Liquor License Application of Vitamin Cottage Natural Food Markets, Inc., dba Natural
Grocers (“Natural Grocers”), for premises at 1851 Dell Range Blvd., Cheyenne, WY 82009
To the Members of the Cheyenne City Council:
Natural Grocers is pleased to present its application for a Retail Liquor License for the City’s consideration.
We are excited at the prospect of bringing our selection of natural, organic and, when possible, local,
alcoholic beverage options to the Cheyenne community.
Natural Grocers has been operating in Cheyenne for over a decade. Over the years we have built a loyal
customer base that values our affordable, highest quality natural and organic grocery items, vitamins and
supplements. This coming August, we are excited to relocate our existing store to 1851 Dell Range Blvd.,
Cheyenne, WY 82009.
With approximately 30% more sales floor area, our relocated Cheyenne location will allow us to offer new
products and services to the community, including a dedicated education center for nutrition education and
other community events. We anticipate employing more than ten additional staff at this store. With
competitive pay and excellent benefits, our new store will offer economic benefits and opportunities to the
Cheyenne community.
In recent years, our company has begun offering a curated selection of alcoholic beverages in select markets.
Our natural, organic and local alcoholic beverage options set us apart from other retailers, and are greatly
valued by our customers. Our floor plan for the relocated Cheyenne store would include floor space for
beer, wine, hard seltzers and hard kombucha products. Should we receive a Retail Liquor License for this
location, as a one-stop shop for our customers’ grocery and alcoholic beverage needs, we believe our store
will be a destination for the community, and will benefit neighboring businesses in the area. Based on
experience, we anticipate the larger new store, with revenues generated from the sale of alcoholic beverages,
would substantially increase our tax base and be a further benefit to the community. As a responsible vendor
who would offer products only for off-premises consumption, our store would not present issues of safety,
noise, over-parking, and similar problems that may be typical of other licensed establishments.
As additional background on our company, Natural Grocers was established in 1955 by Margaret and Philip
Isely, parents of the company’s current leadership. They started the business by going door-to-door in
Golden, Colorado, selling whole-grain bread and sharing nutrition information with their community
members. Over the years, Natural Grocers has grown from a “mom and pop” business to a publicly traded,
160+ store chain with over 3,000 employees. Our success as a company is based on our commitment to our
Vitamin Cottage Natural Food Markets, Inc.
Home Office
• 12612 West Alameda Parkway
• Lakewood, CO 80228
• 303.986.4600
• Fax 303.986.1891
